WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:01.835
UMI

00:01.918 --> 00:04.254
Thanks for working for us for a week!

00:04.337 --> 00:06.297
We really owe you one!

00:06.381 --> 00:08.633
We're going to miss you.

00:08.717 --> 00:10.635
Miku-chan, Hiiragi-san...

00:10.719 --> 00:13.221
Thank you so much for taking care of me!

00:13.304 --> 00:15.098
Pleasure's all ours!

00:15.181 --> 00:16.016
AKANE-CHAN

00:16.099 --> 00:18.309
Here you go.
It's not much, but you earned it.

00:18.393 --> 00:19.728
Thanks!

00:19.811 --> 00:22.147
I have Kyo-chan to thank, but...

00:22.230 --> 00:23.940
You're performing next week, was it?

00:24.023 --> 00:25.108
Uh, yes!

00:25.191 --> 00:28.028
Wait, didn't you say that
you had mid-terms?

00:28.111 --> 00:30.905
What? Can you handle it?

00:30.989 --> 00:32.490
Will you be all right?

00:34.325 --> 00:36.828
Just who do you think I am?

00:36.911 --> 00:40.957
Of course! I'm going to crush them both!

02:12.090 --> 02:13.925
ONE WEEK LATER

02:14.551 --> 02:17.053
FOURTH STORY
BEYOND JOY

02:17.137 --> 02:20.473
Our venue today is a retirement home, huh?

02:20.557 --> 02:21.975
ASSISTED LIVING FACILITY KAGAYAKI

02:22.058 --> 02:24.936
Ah, hello there.

02:25.019 --> 02:26.896
You're the Rakugoka, right?

02:26.980 --> 02:29.190
I'm Tainaka, and I'll be in charge today.

02:29.274 --> 02:31.192
My name is Kyoji Arakawa.

02:31.276 --> 02:33.653
I'm looking forward to today.

02:33.736 --> 02:34.737
My name is Akane.

02:34.821 --> 02:36.406
Thank you for having us.

02:36.489 --> 02:39.200
Please come this way. Oh, I'm so sorry.

02:39.284 --> 02:41.077
No, not at all. Thank you, as always.

02:44.497 --> 02:46.416
Oh, what a sweet child.

02:46.499 --> 02:47.792
The audience today...

02:47.876 --> 02:49.878
They all live here, right?

02:49.961 --> 02:51.254
That's right.

02:51.337 --> 02:55.008
They've asked us to perform today
as part of the facility's recreation.

02:55.091 --> 02:55.967
I see.

02:57.635 --> 02:58.595
Get used to it.

02:59.637 --> 03:02.098
The beauty of Rakugo is that
you can perform anywhere,

03:02.181 --> 03:03.808
as long as there's a cushion.

03:03.892 --> 03:05.852
You may have misgivings about
a strange environment...

03:05.935 --> 03:07.270
Misgivings?

03:07.854 --> 03:08.771
What, you don't?

03:08.855 --> 03:11.482
No, actually, I feel lucky.

03:12.066 --> 03:12.984
Lucky?

03:13.568 --> 03:15.653
It hit me just now.

03:16.613 --> 03:20.366
That today's audience
normally lives this kind of life.

03:21.075 --> 03:25.580
Well, you know how we can only see
the audience when they're at the venue?

03:26.497 --> 03:29.459
So even though it's a given,

03:29.542 --> 03:35.340
I know that they live ordinary lives,
and they're taking the time to see Rakugo.

03:36.007 --> 03:38.009
That's why I'm glad to be at this venue.

03:39.052 --> 03:41.471
I mean, I was raring to go from the start,

03:41.554 --> 03:45.141
but right now, I'm more eager to have them
enjoy themselves.

03:46.392 --> 03:47.393
I see.

03:48.728 --> 03:52.023
That's a good attitude to have, but don't
put too much pressure on yourself.

03:52.106 --> 03:53.107
Uh, right.

03:53.691 --> 03:55.735
I've received permission
from the director.

03:55.818 --> 03:57.570
You'll be taking care of the opening act.

03:57.654 --> 03:59.656
You'll have 15 minutes.

03:59.739 --> 04:01.115
You can do whatever you want.

04:01.199 --> 04:04.035
Your Rakugo performance
that the audience will enjoy...

04:04.118 --> 04:07.205
I'll get a good look
at the answer you arrived at.

04:10.083 --> 04:11.209
Right.

04:11.292 --> 04:13.169
We'll be starting the Rakugo performance.

04:13.253 --> 04:17.799
You've really given me the chance
to learn so much.

04:21.386 --> 04:24.597
So as thanks to you...

04:30.061 --> 04:32.522
I'm going to nail my answer
to your question!

04:39.070 --> 04:41.531
It looks like there are 20 or so people.

04:41.614 --> 04:43.491
And they're all grandpas and grandmas.

04:44.075 --> 04:46.286
Well, of course they are.
It's a retirement home.

04:46.869 --> 04:48.746
My time slot is 15 minutes.

04:48.830 --> 04:51.582
Let's see how much I can have them
enjoy themselves in that time.

04:52.166 --> 04:55.712
If you want people to like you,
then first, you need to accept them!

04:56.504 --> 04:58.256
You're right, Miku-chan!

04:59.048 --> 05:02.010
First, I'll let them get to know me!

05:02.635 --> 05:05.305
So... Hello, my name is Akane.

05:05.388 --> 05:08.349
I'm just a 17-year-old
high school student.

05:09.267 --> 05:12.854
Oh, dear. She's the same age
as my grandchild!

05:12.937 --> 05:14.147
I'll start training...

05:14.230 --> 05:16.983
What? I'm the same age as your grandchild?

05:17.066 --> 05:19.819
If you don't mind my asking,
ma'am, how old are you?

05:19.902 --> 05:21.821
I'm going to be 88 soon.

05:21.904 --> 05:24.198
Oh, 88?

05:24.282 --> 05:26.200
You're so young!

05:26.284 --> 05:29.203
From any angle, you don't look
a day older than 87!

05:30.371 --> 05:34.751
Does anybody else here have grandchildren
in high school?

05:35.543 --> 05:37.378
Oh, so many!

05:37.462 --> 05:40.256
Then I hope you'll see me as
your granddaughter visiting!

05:40.339 --> 05:41.424
And I hope you'll enjoy...

05:41.507 --> 05:42.592
I see what she's doing.

05:42.675 --> 05:44.260
She's trying to get a read

05:44.761 --> 05:46.554
on the atmosphere in this venue.

05:49.265 --> 05:50.475
The Makura.

05:50.558 --> 05:53.644
The small talk and light conversation
before you launch into your story.

05:54.228 --> 05:57.523
It's during this time that Rakugoka
warm up the audience,

05:57.607 --> 05:59.484
and get a feel for them.

05:59.567 --> 06:02.779
I think I've gotten a sense
of this audience's vibe.

06:02.862 --> 06:04.697
All that's left is that person.

06:05.490 --> 06:07.700
Right now, he's the only one
who looks bored.

06:08.284 --> 06:09.452
In that case...

06:09.535 --> 06:14.582
Today I'd like to tell you a story
called "Praising Children."

06:14.665 --> 06:17.752
I'd appreciate it if you could please
bear with me until the end.

06:24.383 --> 06:26.010
Last eye contact?

06:26.094 --> 06:27.220
Right.

06:27.762 --> 06:30.932
You know how they say the eyes
are as eloquent as the mouth?

06:31.015 --> 06:33.601
It's a customer service strategy
that flight attendants use.

06:33.684 --> 06:36.687
You look someone in the eye just as
they're leaving, and give them a smile!

06:36.771 --> 06:38.648
It'll give them a good impression.

06:38.731 --> 06:40.691
Will it go that smoothly?

06:40.775 --> 06:43.653
Of course! Just think about it.

06:43.736 --> 06:45.238
It's not anyone else.

06:45.321 --> 06:47.490
If someone smiles at you alone,

06:47.573 --> 06:50.201
wouldn't that make you
feel special, and happy?

06:52.245 --> 06:54.580
Saburo, get a hold of yourself!

07:01.003 --> 07:02.505
She's like a different person.

07:02.588 --> 07:06.050
Rakugo demands that you have
a conversation with the audience.

07:06.134 --> 07:08.511
Even if you don't exchange words,
there's information you can mine

07:09.095 --> 07:11.514
from gazes, facial expressions,
and the atmosphere.

07:11.597 --> 07:13.766
By reading and empathizing
with their feelings,

07:13.850 --> 07:15.852
you can draw them into your story.

07:15.935 --> 07:19.605
And the only way to do that
is by responding to your audience.

07:19.689 --> 07:22.233
They say that borrowed plumes
will soon come off.

07:22.316 --> 07:26.195
Apparently, mimicking others
doesn't ever go well.

07:26.279 --> 07:29.866
Looks like she learned a lot
at Izakaya Umi. Now...

07:29.949 --> 07:33.453
I'm ready! Now it's starting for real!

07:33.536 --> 07:35.830
Ah, hello, Old Master!

07:35.913 --> 07:37.999
What? Is that you, Hattsan?

07:38.082 --> 07:40.835
Well, never mind that, come on in!

07:40.918 --> 07:42.670
Thank you.

07:42.753 --> 07:44.464
What brings you here today?

07:44.547 --> 07:47.341
Well, I just thought I'd come over
for some of that...

07:48.009 --> 07:49.010
free sake.

07:49.594 --> 07:50.845
What's that?

07:50.928 --> 07:52.930
Come on, you don't have to hide it!

07:53.014 --> 07:58.478
I just heard from someone outside
that you serve sake for free here.

07:58.561 --> 08:01.481
I thought, I could use some free sake!
And so here I am.

08:01.564 --> 08:04.650
Come on, give me a drink, you cheapskate!

08:04.734 --> 08:08.738
Now look here, you sure are being hasty.

08:08.821 --> 08:12.158
As if there were
any free sake in this world!

08:12.241 --> 08:14.827
What I've got here is sake for three.

08:14.911 --> 08:16.871
Not free, but three.

08:16.954 --> 08:18.456
Three and free?

08:18.539 --> 08:20.583
It's the same story,
but it feels so different.

08:20.666 --> 08:22.335
Come on, I came all this way.

08:22.418 --> 08:24.921
PRAISING CHILDREN

08:25.004 --> 08:26.005
"Praising Children."

08:27.048 --> 08:29.800
In this Zenza-banashi,
Hachigoro pesters the Old Master

08:29.884 --> 08:33.554
for free drinks, but instead, he's taught
how to compliment others.

08:33.638 --> 08:36.599
Since he wasn't paying attention,
he keeps falling flat.

08:37.225 --> 08:38.851
Oh, I get it.

08:38.935 --> 08:42.688
If a 45-year-old comes along,
you say, "You look so young for 45."

08:42.772 --> 08:45.483
"You only look maybe around 100!"

08:45.566 --> 08:47.401
No, I said, younger than 45!

08:48.236 --> 08:49.278
What's that now?

08:49.362 --> 08:51.656
You don't know anything, do you?

08:51.739 --> 08:53.950
For a man of 45, that's about 42 or so!

08:54.033 --> 08:56.661
If you tell a 45-year-old
that he looks 42...

08:57.703 --> 08:59.580
A slow tempo.

08:59.664 --> 09:01.958
Just right for today's audience.

09:02.792 --> 09:07.380
Only a Rakugoka can adjust
her storytelling to suit her audience.

09:07.463 --> 09:09.298
So she's building on her last experience.

09:10.216 --> 09:12.301
Looks like I can watch her today
with no qualms.

09:13.970 --> 09:16.347
What do I do if I see someone who's 50?

09:16.430 --> 09:20.184
Well, then you tell him he looks like he's
45 or 46.

09:20.268 --> 09:22.812
Okay... And if the person is 60?

09:22.895 --> 09:24.814
Well, then 55 or 56.

09:24.897 --> 09:26.941
Oh, is that right? How about 70?

09:27.024 --> 09:28.150
Yeah, 65 or 66.

09:28.234 --> 09:29.193
And 80?

09:29.277 --> 09:30.695
Ugh, 75 or 76.

09:30.778 --> 09:31.696
And 90?

09:31.779 --> 09:33.781
Say 85 or 86.

09:33.864 --> 09:34.657
And 100?

09:36.576 --> 09:38.995
Is she increasing the tempo?

09:39.078 --> 09:42.081
Like a car shifting into higher gear,
gradually accelerating...

09:42.164 --> 09:44.500
She's increasing the tempo of her story,
bit by bit.

09:44.584 --> 09:47.169
Maybe say 95 or 96?

09:47.253 --> 09:50.006
The audience hasn't realized
that the tempo's faster.

09:50.506 --> 09:52.049
Don't tell me...

09:52.133 --> 09:55.386
In order to make sure they'd enjoy it
even at the tempo of your choice...

09:55.469 --> 09:57.805
You got them used to it?

10:00.891 --> 10:01.684
What?

10:01.767 --> 10:04.020
You even make your own mayonnaise?

10:04.103 --> 10:05.730
Talk about passionate!

10:05.813 --> 10:07.440
Of course!

10:07.523 --> 10:10.151
First and foremost,
the customer needs to be happy.

10:10.234 --> 10:14.071
And second, I need to serve them food
that I can be proud of!

10:14.655 --> 10:16.032
What a surprise.

10:17.074 --> 10:19.285
Attentiveness, eh?

10:19.368 --> 10:22.330
Well, I'm sure Akane will do just fine.

10:23.039 --> 10:26.542
With all due respect,
she seemed to be brooding.

10:26.626 --> 10:32.423
See, Akane is someone who can think
about others, care for them, and learn.

10:33.215 --> 10:37.678
Seems like an apprentice from another
school's got her worked up lately,

10:39.513 --> 10:40.931
but there's nothing to worry about.

10:41.474 --> 10:44.977
Those eyes will surely reach the audience.

10:45.895 --> 10:47.229
Thank goodness.

10:47.313 --> 10:50.191
My storytelling is making
the audience laugh.

10:50.274 --> 10:52.318
I'm so thrilled!

10:52.902 --> 10:54.070
Also, "Praising Children"

10:54.153 --> 10:57.239
is a tale about a man who didn't listen
to what someone was teaching him.

10:57.323 --> 10:59.075
He was a know-it-all
but he kept messing up.

10:59.659 --> 11:03.371
I think in a lot of ways,
that's exactly how I've been lately.

11:03.454 --> 11:06.123
This story really hit home for me.

11:06.916 --> 11:09.919
Come to think of it,
years ago, the master...

11:15.383 --> 11:21.430
Listen, Akane, Rakugo is an art form
created by the townspeople of that era.

11:21.514 --> 11:25.059
That's one reason why the characters
are carpenters, fishermen,

11:25.142 --> 11:27.395
landlords who rent out homes...

11:27.478 --> 11:30.189
They were ordinary people, just like us.

11:31.357 --> 11:36.237
So you'll one day come to understand
how the people in your stories felt.

11:37.363 --> 11:40.616
Will I understand
how people from long ago felt?

11:40.699 --> 11:42.201
Sure you will.

11:43.202 --> 11:49.834
Being human and how people think
hasn't changed at all, no matter the era.

11:51.335 --> 11:54.505
So Akane, I hope you'll experience
all kinds of things.

11:54.588 --> 11:56.006
Agonize as much as you want.

11:56.090 --> 11:57.716
Get hurt a lot.

11:58.300 --> 12:02.471
And one day for sure,
all of that will fuel your stories.

12:05.808 --> 12:08.477
At the time,
I didn't really get what he meant.

12:09.645 --> 12:11.188
But now I know.

12:12.189 --> 12:16.485
My experiences from back then
are connected to this moment right now!

12:17.027 --> 12:19.530
I'm sure nothing went to waste.

12:20.030 --> 12:23.576
Every bit of it is an asset to my Rakugo.

12:25.578 --> 12:26.912
How old, did you say?

12:26.996 --> 12:29.707
He was just born, so he's one.

12:29.790 --> 12:31.167
One? Hey!

12:31.250 --> 12:33.002
For one, he looks really young!

12:33.085 --> 12:36.964
You idiot, if he looks young for one,
how the heck old would that be?

12:37.047 --> 12:39.675
He couldn't be more than half.

12:47.975 --> 12:49.185
Amazing.

12:51.562 --> 12:55.399
Rakugo is so much fun!

13:04.074 --> 13:05.743
I hardly recognized you.

13:05.826 --> 13:07.286
I was truly stunned.

13:07.870 --> 13:09.997
Keep that up
and apply yourself to your training.

13:10.080 --> 13:11.999
Thank you very much!

13:13.209 --> 13:14.710
What are you thanking me for?

13:14.793 --> 13:16.462
For everything.

13:17.421 --> 13:21.217
I understand how narrow
my perspective was until now.

13:21.717 --> 13:26.639
I think I've started liking Rakugo
even a little more now.

13:27.723 --> 13:28.599
Is that right?

13:29.225 --> 13:32.144
I'm not sure what you mean,
but if I was helpful, I'm glad.

13:33.354 --> 13:36.357
I got a good look at your answer.

13:36.440 --> 13:38.526
Now it's my turn to captivate you.

13:39.693 --> 13:43.197
I'm going to show you how imposing
your elder fellow apprentice is!

13:47.326 --> 13:51.121
At the last two-man show, I was so busy
with chores in the dressing room,

13:51.205 --> 13:52.957
that I didn't get a good look.

13:58.837 --> 14:02.841
This is my first time
watching Kyoji-san's performance.

14:04.677 --> 14:06.804
My name is Kyoji Arakawa.

14:07.638 --> 14:09.765
The way he sits is so beautiful.

14:10.349 --> 14:12.851
Just having great posture
is enough to rivet you.

14:12.935 --> 14:15.354
...Edokko,
those who were born and raised in Edo.

14:15.437 --> 14:18.816
No true Edokko saves his money.
They had no fixation on getting rich...

14:18.899 --> 14:20.901
She answered my question with aplomb.

14:21.819 --> 14:23.362
Now, it's my turn.

14:23.946 --> 14:28.367
What can I show her from up here?

14:28.450 --> 14:32.496
Seems like they were quite
a carefree bunch.

14:32.997 --> 14:34.707
Oh, come on.

14:34.790 --> 14:37.209
Why did I have to find
something like this?

14:37.293 --> 14:38.919
I found a wallet.

14:39.003 --> 14:42.047
I look inside and there's three ryo,
an official document, and a seal.

14:42.131 --> 14:45.467
It says here, Kanda Tate Daikucho,
Kichigoro, the carpenter.

14:45.551 --> 14:46.635
This story...

14:47.553 --> 14:49.346
It's "Three Men Lose One Ryo."

14:50.264 --> 14:52.182
Kintaro finds a wallet in the street.

14:52.266 --> 14:55.394
Using the official document
and seal inside,

14:55.477 --> 14:58.063
he tracks down the owner, Kichigoro,
and delivers it to him.

14:58.147 --> 15:01.775
But no true Edokko would save his money
for tomorrow.

15:02.276 --> 15:06.572
Faced with the lost three ryo,
neither man would bend their will.

15:07.072 --> 15:08.198
Here it is.

15:08.282 --> 15:11.911
Oh, I see, there's a Kichi
inside the circle.

15:13.329 --> 15:16.081
Yeah, but I just hope
this damned guy is here.

15:16.165 --> 15:19.460
If he's not around, I'd look like a fool
holding this thing.

15:19.543 --> 15:22.296
What's this? Looks like he just repapered
his shoji screens.

15:22.379 --> 15:23.714
Why don't I just check for myself.

15:23.797 --> 15:24.632
Here we go!

15:24.715 --> 15:27.426
Uh, so what's the situation?

15:28.093 --> 15:29.261
Hey, there he is.

15:29.345 --> 15:30.930
Right, so that's the Kichi dude.

15:31.013 --> 15:34.475
Every word and gesture is meticulous.

15:34.558 --> 15:37.102
His Rakugo is perfectly executed
and serious.

15:38.395 --> 15:42.524
Hey! A real Edokko would pair his sake
with something less savory!

15:44.693 --> 15:45.861
Some weird guy just showed up.

15:46.862 --> 15:49.698
Hey, you're the carpenter,
Kichigoro, right?

15:49.782 --> 15:50.908
That's right.

15:50.991 --> 15:53.661
I'm a carpenter, and my name is Kichigoro.
Who the heck are you?

15:53.744 --> 15:56.580
Me? I'm Kintaro the plasterer.

15:56.664 --> 15:59.083
Kintaro, you say?
For a Kintaro, you're not that red.

15:59.166 --> 16:02.920
I get it. Kyoji-san's not just serious.

16:03.003 --> 16:04.046
Listen, you!

16:04.129 --> 16:06.006
He's too serious!

16:06.090 --> 16:08.842
I came all this way to give it
back to you.

16:08.926 --> 16:09.969
Go on, take it!

16:11.679 --> 16:13.722
What did you go and do that for?

16:13.806 --> 16:15.683
You bastard! Damn you!

16:15.766 --> 16:18.602
Listen, I didn't
leave this wallet there, okay?

16:18.686 --> 16:20.312
I dropped it, all right?

16:20.396 --> 16:23.357
Whether I dropped it at Yanagiwara
or some other place, I couldn't care less!

16:23.440 --> 16:25.734
You couldn't care less?

16:25.818 --> 16:28.112
Look, your name is on this document, see?

16:28.195 --> 16:29.279
Shut up, you jerk!

16:29.363 --> 16:31.865
I don't want that money.
I'm giving it to you, so take it!

16:31.949 --> 16:34.368
I'm getting a beat-down
for returning your money?

16:34.451 --> 16:35.995
How ridiculous is that?

16:36.078 --> 16:37.454
- How dare you!
- Shut up!

16:37.538 --> 16:39.665
The Rakugo dialogue itself is comical.

16:39.748 --> 16:42.209
But if he delivers it so seriously,
it'll make me laugh!

16:42.292 --> 16:45.796
Oh, no! Another ruckus started next door.

16:45.879 --> 16:48.799
Hey, Mr. Landlord! Mr. Landlord!

16:49.383 --> 16:50.342
Kyoji.

16:51.051 --> 16:53.929
You shouldn't try to make people laugh.

16:54.013 --> 17:00.102
You're not adroit enough to make people
laugh at your witty wordplay, are you?

17:00.185 --> 17:01.812
Be serious.

17:02.771 --> 17:06.316
If I may, Master, just being serious
won't get any laughs.

17:06.400 --> 17:08.944
True, just being serious would be boring.

17:09.028 --> 17:09.862
But you know what?

17:09.945 --> 17:12.322
If you're too serious, it'll be funny.

17:13.490 --> 17:15.576
If it's exceptional,
that'll be your uniqueness.

17:15.659 --> 17:16.994
Be stubbornly honest.

17:17.077 --> 17:19.705
That will be your weapon.

17:19.788 --> 17:22.207
And so, the matter of the three ryo,

17:22.291 --> 17:25.586
which had sparked this spat
between Kichigoro and Kintaro,

17:25.669 --> 17:28.172
was sent before
the honorable Ooka Echizen,

17:28.255 --> 17:30.674
Magistrate of South Edo for his ruling.

17:31.258 --> 17:32.342
Kichigoro.

17:32.426 --> 17:35.387
I understand that when this Kintaro came
to deliver the wallet you had lost,

17:35.471 --> 17:38.098
you flew into a rage and struck him.

17:38.182 --> 17:39.516
Is that correct?

17:40.100 --> 17:41.393
That's correct, but please understand,

17:41.477 --> 17:44.271
I have no intention of accepting money
that I'd dropped,

17:44.354 --> 17:45.898
so I told him, "You take it instead!"

17:46.482 --> 17:47.441
Is that so?

17:47.941 --> 17:48.901
Kintaro.

17:48.984 --> 17:51.904
Why did you not accept
his offer of three ryo?

17:52.488 --> 17:54.031
Are you kidding me, your honor?

17:54.114 --> 17:57.493
It's our job to teach society the virtue
of returning lost items to their owners!

17:57.576 --> 17:59.661
I'm not some tightwad who'd pounce
on someone else's three ryo!

18:00.370 --> 18:01.914
Is that so?

18:01.997 --> 18:06.794
So you're telling me that neither of you
is willing to accept this money?

18:07.836 --> 18:11.340
The relationship between a Rakugo master
and his apprentices is a strange one.

18:12.132 --> 18:13.926
Just because a master takes on apprentices

18:14.009 --> 18:16.011
that doesn't mean he gains anything.

18:17.012 --> 18:21.266
In fact, from teaching etiquette
to Rakugo training,

18:21.767 --> 18:23.477
and so many other things...

18:23.977 --> 18:25.437
All he does is give.

18:26.313 --> 18:27.314
But even so...

18:30.692 --> 18:34.738
I have heard both your arguments, and
now I, Echizen, will deliver my verdict.

18:35.239 --> 18:37.950
The three ryo
at the center of this dispute...

18:38.033 --> 18:40.077
I will hold onto them for you.

18:40.160 --> 18:44.998
And now, I shall give both
Kichigoro and Kintaro a reward!

18:46.166 --> 18:49.670
This is to thank you for your display
of Edokko generosity.

18:49.753 --> 18:53.757
And even so, the master cares for us
as if we were his own children,

18:53.841 --> 18:57.177
and with no regard for gain or loss,
he's always looking after us.

18:57.803 --> 18:59.596
I can't even begin to thank him.

19:01.890 --> 19:04.977
All right, now pick up
from where you left off.

19:05.060 --> 19:06.019
Yes.

19:06.728 --> 19:09.648
If Kichigoro had taken the money that
Kintaro returned to him,

19:09.731 --> 19:11.692
he would've had three ryo.

19:11.775 --> 19:14.027
And if Kintaro had taken the money

19:14.111 --> 19:16.071
that was offered to him,
he would've had three ryo.

19:16.155 --> 19:19.491
I will add one ryo to the three
that I'm holding for you,

19:19.575 --> 19:22.452
and by handing you each two ryo...

19:22.536 --> 19:26.415
Let me, as her elder fellow apprentice,
give generously to her.

19:27.124 --> 19:29.042
Just like the master did for me.

19:29.668 --> 19:32.880
And I'll keep being someone
who's capable of giving.

19:33.672 --> 19:36.717
I'll become someone who harbors words,

19:37.593 --> 19:38.719
as a person,

19:39.553 --> 19:40.721
as a Rakugoka,

19:41.305 --> 19:43.390
I'll move forward, and show you...

19:43.891 --> 19:47.394
the example of the kind of elder fellow
apprentice that you'll want to pursue!

19:49.104 --> 19:50.731
And thus, my judgment is...

19:52.441 --> 19:55.194
three men lose one ryo each!

19:56.778 --> 19:58.030
Amazing.

20:03.869 --> 20:07.039
So this is Kyoji-san's Rakugo!

20:11.919 --> 20:14.880
Oh, wow, so it was a roaring success.

20:14.963 --> 20:16.548
Good for you!

20:16.632 --> 20:17.841
I know!

20:17.925 --> 20:20.093
And Kyoji-san's Rakugo
was incredible, too!

20:21.220 --> 20:24.306
Hey, I used all the customer service
that I learned here in my Makura...

20:24.389 --> 20:25.307
I just remembered.

20:25.807 --> 20:27.351
I have no problem with it,

20:27.434 --> 20:30.729
but there are some who frown upon
the opening act starting with a Makura,

20:30.812 --> 20:31.939
so be careful.

20:32.022 --> 20:32.898
Right!

20:35.067 --> 20:35.984
One more thing.

20:36.068 --> 20:38.195
From now on, call me Kyoji Ani-san.

20:39.905 --> 20:42.199
Did you say Ani-san?

20:42.282 --> 20:43.200
That's right.

20:43.951 --> 20:45.077
Being taken on as an apprentice

20:45.160 --> 20:48.121
is like starting a parent-child
relationship with your master.

20:48.205 --> 20:51.583
The master is our parent, and
his apprentices are all his children.

20:51.667 --> 20:54.127
You don't use honorifics
for your siblings, do you?

20:54.211 --> 20:59.132
Rakugoka call their close seniors
Ani-san or Nee-san.

21:00.008 --> 21:01.635
Got that, Akane?

21:02.928 --> 21:05.097
It's not inward that
you need to gaze into right now.

21:05.180 --> 21:08.558
I got a good look at your answer.

21:09.476 --> 21:11.353
For the first time,
he called me by my name.

21:11.853 --> 21:12.688
Right.

21:14.273 --> 21:17.192
Thank you for teaching me, Kyoji Ani-san!

21:17.276 --> 21:19.194
Yes. Well done.

21:21.029 --> 21:23.407
Isn't this great? Like the joys of youth!

21:23.490 --> 21:28.203
Hey, come to think of it,
are your midterms going well?

21:28.287 --> 21:29.454
Oh shoot.

21:29.538 --> 21:30.747
Oh shoot...

21:30.831 --> 21:32.207
Oh shoot?

21:32.791 --> 21:35.043
Just what is going on here?

21:36.253 --> 21:37.838
No, no, it's just...

21:37.921 --> 21:41.466
Hey, I was thinking I should start
working on that, you know?

21:41.550 --> 21:44.594
You little fool!

21:45.095 --> 21:48.724
Didn't I tell you that while you're
in school, your studies come first?

21:48.807 --> 21:50.976
I forbid you from accompanying me
during your mid-terms!

21:51.059 --> 21:52.352
Hit the books!

21:52.436 --> 21:55.439
Starting tomorrow,
bring your notebook every day!

21:55.522 --> 21:56.523
No need to be shy!

21:56.606 --> 21:58.233
How did it come to this?

21:58.317 --> 21:59.735
I don't know either.

21:59.818 --> 22:01.194
Hey! Are you listening?

22:01.278 --> 22:02.946
Ah, youth!

23:36.248 --> 23:37.916
NEXT EPISODE
HER PATH FORWARD

23:38.792 --> 23:40.460
Akane Small Talk!

23:44.464 --> 23:45.507
Kyoji Ani-san!

23:45.590 --> 23:49.136
Calling you "Ani-san"
makes me feel a lot closer to you.

23:49.219 --> 23:50.095
Right.

23:50.178 --> 23:52.889
Being in the same school
is like being in the same family.

23:52.973 --> 23:55.225
- You should have a stronger sense of that.
- Right!

23:55.308 --> 23:59.563
Still, it's also customary for Rakugoka
to call their seniors from other schools

23:59.646 --> 24:03.066
Ani-san or Nee-san.

24:03.150 --> 24:06.319
And another thing that sets us apart
from Kamigata Rakugo

24:06.403 --> 24:08.947
is the fact that they say
Nii-san rather than Ani-san.

24:09.030 --> 24:10.532
Really?

24:10.615 --> 24:13.618
However, that's only
up to the Futatsume rank.

24:13.702 --> 24:15.704
In some cases, it would be considered rude

24:15.787 --> 24:18.331
not to call elder fellow apprentices
promoted to Shin'uchi as "Master,"

24:18.415 --> 24:20.542
- so watch out.
- I'll keep that in mind!

24:20.625 --> 24:21.793
One more thing.

24:21.877 --> 24:25.422
You would call a master
from another school "Master So-and-so,"

24:25.505 --> 24:27.007
but when referring to your own master,

24:27.090 --> 24:30.760
you'd just call him "Master"
or "my master."

24:31.261 --> 24:34.764
If you think about the relationship
between master and apprentice being like

24:34.848 --> 24:36.474
a parent and child, it should make sense.

24:36.558 --> 24:37.559
I get it!

24:37.642 --> 24:40.478
I call my own father "Dad,"

24:40.562 --> 24:43.732
but if it's my friend's father,
I say "So-and-so's dad."

24:43.815 --> 24:44.941
You little fool!

24:45.025 --> 24:49.529
You wouldn't call someone else's father
her "dad," you'd say her "father"!

24:49.613 --> 24:51.448
R-Right.
